  {
   "text": "I designed the spinner as a 75 mm three-lobe part, 8 mm thick, and added it to the project as \"Three lobe fidget spinner 75 mm with print in place hub.\" It measures 75 x 68.2 mm. The 75 mm span is tip to tip across the two lower lobes, and the top lobe is shorter, so the outline is not a true circle. My first attempt measured 67.9 mm, so I rescaled the outline to hit 75.\n\nThe hub is a 22.1 mm disc sitting in a 23 mm bore, leaving a 0.45 mm radial gap. Nothing ties it to the body, so it spins freely by hand but can fall out. For a fidget that stays together, the next step is a retaining cap or flange, which I can add if you want it. The gap is small for the P1S with a 0.4 mm nozzle, so the first layer may fuse it shut. A slightly larger gap, around 0.5 mm, is safer if the hub binds after printing.\n\nNothing has been sliced or sent to the printer. Say the word and I'll slice it on your P1S with PLA and queue it."
